Lab: Workstation Ethernet Connectivity 

Objective

Configure and connect the workstation to the LAN and to the Internet.

Environment

Tools Used

Cat6a Cable w/RJ45

Operating System

Windows 11 Pro

Skills Practiced

Patch Panel Installation
System configuration

Actions Performed

Identified and connected the workstation port on the patch panel to the port on the Cisco Switch using a Cat6a Cable w/RJ45
Connected the desktop NIC port to the RJ45 wall jack using a Cat6a Cable w/RJ45
Changed the DHCP/DNS setting in Network & Internet Settings from Manual to Automatic
Visually confirmed connectivity in the Network & Internet Settings 
Pinged External DNS Servers to verify connectivity
Documented findings

Commands Used

Ping

Verification

Visually confirmed connectivity in the Internet Setting & Pinged the External DNS Servers for confirmation.

Issues Encountered

None

Resolution

The workstation was connected to the LAN and Internet by connecting the desktop to the wall port, then the patch panel, and to the switch. 
This completed the physical connection. Configured the settings properly to allow for a digital connection with verification, 
ensuring the workstation was properly set up.

Key Takeaways

Verify all physical connections are properly connected and labeled before working on settings 
Visual confirmation is useful. The correct way is to utilize tools to verify that the connection is active.

